Week–1: Install Apache Kafka on a Single Node

For your Lab Internal Exam, you can write the following short and easy version. It is directly based on the Week-1 material in your file.

Aim

To install Apache Kafka on a single node using Docker.

Commands
docker pull wurstmeister/zookeeper
docker pull wurstmeister/kafka
Start Zookeeper
docker run -d --name zookeeper -p 2181:2181 wurstmeister/zookeeper
Start Kafka
docker run -d --name kafka -p 9092:9092 --link zookeeper:zookeeper \
-e KAFKA_ZOOKEEPER_CONNECT=zookeeper:2181 \
-e KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://localhost:9092 \
-e KAFKA_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://0.0.0.0:9092 \
wurstmeister/kafka
Result

Apache Kafka was successfully installed and started on a single node using Docker.

🧠 Easy order to remember

Pull → Zookeeper → Kafka

1. docker pull Zookeeper
2. docker pull Kafka
3. Run Zookeeper
4. Run Kafka
